Activity 4
What is a Framework?
A framework is a structured plan or system that outlines specific actions, policies, and technologies to address a particular goal - in this case, ensuring privacy. It includes:
•	Features: The tools and technical measures to ensure data privacy (e.g., encryption).
•	Policies: The rules or practices for how data is handled, accessed, and stored.
•	Compliance: Steps to meet legal and ethical standards.
•	Presentation Tips: Clearly organise your framework into sections for features, policies, compliance, and alignment with user needs. Use bullet points or a flowchart for clarity.
Task:
•	Review the scenario below about a mobile health app.
•	Identify key privacy considerations and challenges.
•	Collaboratively design a privacy-by-design framework.
•	Summarise your framework in a visual format (e.g., bullet points, table, or diagram) and prepare to present it in 2 minutes to the class.

Time Allocation:
•	20 minutes: Collaborate and design your framework.
•	5 minutes: Summarise and present your framework.
Scenario
Title: Privacy-by-Design for a Mobile Health Application
Your team has been tasked with designing a privacy-by-design framework for a mobile health app, "HealthSync," that tracks users' fitness, diet, and medical records. The app collects sensitive personal data such as heart rate, calorie intake, and medical history, which it shares with healthcare providers to improve user health outcomes.
Key challenges include:
1.	Protecting sensitive health data from unauthorised access or breaches.
2.	Ensuring user consent for data collection, sharing, and usage.
3.	Maintaining compliance with GDPR and HIPAA requirements.
4.	Balancing data minimisation with providing comprehensive health insights.
The framework must include:
•	Privacy features (e.g., encryption, user controls).
•	Organisational policies for data governance.
•	Strategies to align with user and regulatory requirements.
Discussion Points
