What are Privacy Features? 
Privacy features are tools and techniques designed to protect sensitive data, ensure compliance with regulations, and uphold user trust. These include: 
•	Data Minimisation: Only collecting and storing the data strictly necessary for a task. 
•	Secure Processing: Using measures like encryption, access control, and regular audits to safeguard data. 
•	Practical Integration: Embedding these features into applications during design and implementation stages.

